      "id": 5609,
      "name": "EvanDan55",
      "username": "EvanDan55",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-13T13:42:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It actually took a while for me to realize what was different about the new environments: they have pictures (how I didn’t notice this immediately, I’ll never know). But besides me missing that obvious fact, it got me wondering, will Adam be making new pictures for the core environments, and then a remastered version of the core environments with those pictures be released for purchase in the store? I’d totally pay $12 (assuming prices of environments in the store don’t change) to have new, prettier core environments.</p>\n<p>Oh, and I almost forgot: besides the wonderful new pictures on the business end of the cards, maybe they could also have new, uniform backs for the entire deck, like how the RC environments have a shot of the actual area and the name of the environment on there. Something like (for example) a shot of Atlantas in the mid and background, and a fallen archway with “Atlantas” on it in the foreground.</p>\n<p>I know the core environments already do have custom uniform backs with fancy titles, but that doesn’t mean they can’t be spiced up, since they all have the same backdrop.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:18.552Z",
